  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 215 AM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nThe hot and dry conditions will continue through at least the end\nof the week with deterministic and ensemble NWP in agreement the \nsubtropical ridge will continue to be the primary influence of our\nweather. High temperatures will continue to range from the upper \n90s to the mid 100s deg F. With the ongoing drought and dry fuels,\nfire weather will also continue to be a concern. \n\nEnsemble spread does begin to increase by the Labor Day weekend \nwith some members indicating the ridge may retrograde to the west \nto allow a backdoor cold front to be in close proximity with less \nhot weather. For example, the probabilistic National Blend of \nModels (NBM) forecast has around an 8 to 15 deg F spread between \nthe 10th and 90th percentile temperatures on Labor Day. The 10th \npercentile temperature forecast is in the upper 80s (north) to \nupper 90s (south) deg F. However, the more likely scenario as of \nnow is that the heat wave will continue.\n\nMahale",
